{
  "requirement": "`verify` always captures `Some(criterion.version())`. When `load_evidence` loads\nan older answer with no known version, `Fingerprinted::version()` returns `None`.\n`Record::version` holds the same optional value. In the serialized `revision`\nfield, a concrete string represents `Some(version)` and `\"*\"` represents `None`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: **Structural obligations**\n\n- Clause: \"`Record::version` holds the same optional value.\" This prescribes a field and its type. An implementation could store a plain `String` such as `\"*\"` in `Record`. It could behave the same at runtime, but `Record::version` would no longer hold the optional value. The obligation is structural, and `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#struct[Record]` meets it. Its `version` field is `Option<CriterionVersion>`.\n- Clause: \"In the serialized `revision` field, a concrete string represents `Some(version)` and `\\\"*\\\"` represents `None`.\" This constrains the type's serialized form. `Record` declares `#[serde(rename = \"revision\", with = \"stored_version\")]` on `version`. The helpers it reaches are in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#mod[stored_version]`:\n  - `fn[serialize]` writes `\"*\"` for `None` and the version string for `Some`.\n  - `fn[deserialize]` goes through `CriterionVersion::from_recorded`. I did not read that function.\n  Because `Record` reaches these helpers through its serde attribute, they need no marker of their own.\n\n**Behavioral clauses, not structural**\n\n- \"`verify` always captures `Some(criterion.version())`.\" This is observable behavior. `Validator::execute` sets `version: Some(version)` when it builds the `Fingerprinted`. A different internal design that records the same value would still satisfy the text.\n- \"When `load_evidence` loads an older answer with no known version, `Fingerprinted::version()` returns `None`.\" This is also observable behavior. `load_evidence` copies `record.version` into the `Fingerprinted`, and `Fingerprinted::version` returns it through `as_ref()`. A `Fingerprinted` that stored the version differently but returned `None` here would behave identically. The accessor and the loader are therefore discretionary, and they need no implementation roots of their own.\n\nThe single supplied root, `Record`, covers every structural clause, and no other root is needed. There are no acknowledgments.\n\nbehavioral: The tests cover every observable obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.recorded_criterion_version`.\n\n1. **`verify` always captures `Some(criterion.version())`.**\n   - `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` (`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs`) asserts `value.version().unwrap().as_str() == \"v1\"`. It also asserts that the loaded version equals the verified one after `store_evidence`.\n   - `typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence` (same file) verifies with revision \"v2\" and asserts `Some(\"v2\")`. It also asserts the stored record keeps \"v1\" until the new value is explicitly stored.\n   - `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records` (same file) asserts that each stored `Record::version` is the revision of the execution that produced it (\"first-revision\" or \"second-revision\").\n\n2. **`load_evidence` of an older answer with no known version makes `Fingerprinted::version()` return `None`.**\n   - `wildcard_revision_does_not_supply_other_criteria_or_nodes` (same file) sets the stored record's version to `None`. It loads the record and asserts `loaded.version() == None`.\n\n3. **`Record::version` holds the same optional value, and the serialized `revision` field uses a concrete string for `Some` and `\"*\"` for `None`.**\n   - `record_preserves_the_stored_version_encoding` (`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs`) deserializes both `\"review-v1\"` and `\"*\"`. It asserts `Some(\"review-v1\")` and `None` respectively, then asserts the serialized value equals the original wire JSON. It also asserts that `\"*\"` is not a valid `CriterionVersion`.\n\nAll these tests carry `{test}` references to the subject. I found no missing scenario or weak assertion.",
