        "rationale": "The tests cover every observable obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.recorded_criterion_version`.\n\n1. **`verify` always captures `Some(criterion.version())`.**\n   - `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` (`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs`) asserts `value.version().unwrap().as_str() == \"v1\"`. It also asserts that the loaded version equals the verified one after `store_evidence`.\n   - `typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence` (same file) verifies with revision \"v2\" and asserts `Some(\"v2\")`. It also asserts the stored record keeps \"v1\" until the new value is explicitly stored.\n   - `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records` (same file) asserts that each stored `Record::version` is the revision of the execution that produced it (\"first-revision\" or \"second-revision\").\n\n2. **`load_evidence` of an older answer with no known version makes `Fingerprinted::version()` return `None`.**\n   - `wildcard_revision_does_not_supply_other_criteria_or_nodes` (same file) sets the stored record's version to `None`. It loads the record and asserts `loaded.version() == None`.\n\n3. **`Record::version` holds the same optional value, and the serialized `revision` field uses a concrete string for `Some` and `\"*\"` for `None`.**\n   - `record_preserves_the_stored_version_encoding` (`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs`) deserializes both `\"review-v1\"` and `\"*\"`. It asserts `Some(\"review-v1\")` and `None` respectively, then asserts the serialized value equals the original wire JSON. It also asserts that `\"*\"` is not a valid `CriterionVersion`.\n\nAll these tests carry `{test}` references to the subject. I found no missing scenario or weak assertion."
